 "title": "Handling the 'I'll get back to you' client objection",
 "topic": "sales",
 "summary": "This video outlines a strategy for overcoming the 'I'll get back to you' client objection. The creator advises asking clarifying questions to identify if the issue is a lack of priority or a budget concern, then presenting a low-risk, results-based pilot approach.",
 "key_points": [
  "When a client says 'I will get back to you', ask if the issue is a lack of priority or a budget concern.",
  "Address the objection by offering a low-risk test run (e.g., a one-month trial) to prove results.",
  "Explain the potential return on investment for the trial period, even in a worst-case scenario.",
  "If the client has a team, offer to train them on your strategies to implement and drive results.",
  "Use the results from the trial period as a foundation for further scaling discussions."
 ],
 "content": "Caption: Comment \"19\" and I'll share the most common objections and how to handle to close a deal on the call. Transcript: (Creator) So, the price for a 3-month package would be 3 lakh rupees. (Client) Okay, give me some time, I will get back to you. (Creator) Sure, but before actually we end this call, can I ask you one question? (Client) Sure. (Creator) Okay, when usually people say that they will get back, it is actually because of these two reasons, okay? Either this solution right now is not the priority, or the budget is actually the concern. So, which one is it for you? (Client) See, I would say both. I am not sure how it's going to work for my industry and it's so much for me to invest. (Creator) Okay, got it. So let's say this solution is going to add you 10 calls, a bare minimum, okay? And you end up closing two calls out of it. And as you are already charging like 2k per month, per deal you are closing, you will anyway be making 4k a month. And if you, in case sign a 3-month contract with them, it will be 12k of a deal size. I'm talking about the worst-case scenario here. The best case would be like you closing three or more sales and it is the investment of just 1k. So, would it still feel like the kind of transformation you would sign up for? Why I'm asking is because you're already getting five low-quality leads, right, which doesn't close. The probability of you making money is actually less. (Client) I understand, but I am not in the position to invest that much money. My budget is only [unclear]. If you can work on that for a month, then we can upgrade for the next month. I can literally work on that [unclear] budget. (Creator) Okay, do you have a team? (Client) Yes. (Creator) Okay, what I can do is actually come in and train your team. I'll give them the strategies to implement. They implement what I'm saying, they bring the results, and initially, as I have asked for the test, we are going to go aim for like one call close. You are going to get five calls a month, try closing at least one and you'll be making 2k as we have already discussed. Once you see the results coming in, we can talk about scaling part later. Text on screen: CLIENT OBJECTION: I'll get back to you",
